Description:

A JMAP sharee with mayWriteOwn on another user's calendar can now update or
destroy only the events that the sharee organizes.  Previously,
CalendarEvent/set compared each event's organizer against the calendar owner's
addresses rather than the sharee's, so every event in the calendar counted as
the sharee's own, and the sharee could rewrite owner-controlled fields (title,
timing, location, etc.) of any of them, or destroy them.

Reported by: Michael Lynch (mtlynch.io).


CVE number:

CVE-2026-61914
Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-45q6-9pg6-h3xw.


CVE description:

Write-own calendar share permits altering any event

An authenticated JMAP user permitted to change only their own events in
another user's shared calendar could modify or delete any event in that
calendar.


